WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:12.340
97. American Football. Huge men sprint across the field like gazelles, then smash into each

2
00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:19.500
other like trains. One man is alone, inside a clear space, while other men fight to protect

3
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:25.600
him. Just before he falls under the weight of other bodies, he throws a ball high into

4
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:33.640
the air. Thirty yards away, it is caught. A touchdown. The crowd goes wild. This is

5
00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:39.280
American football. It's the most popular sport in the United States, but it's not well-known

6
00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:46.600
elsewhere. Two teams of 11 men fight to move along a hundred-yard field. Each team defends

7
00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:53.480
its goal at the ends of the field. The men try to move a ball. The ball can be thrown,

8
00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:59.000
played, or kicked. A team scores six points for carrying or throwing the ball across the

9
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.880
other team's goal line, and three points for kicking the ball between the other team's

10
00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:11.960
goal posts. American football, called football in the United States, evolved in the nineteenth

11
00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:17.800
century from different types of rugby which is played in the United Kingdom. Rugby has

12
00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:24.400
a similar ball and similar rules to football. While American football is still clearly related

13
00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:32.440
to rugby, the two games are now very different. American football was already a popular high

14
00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:39.720
school and college game before it was recognized as a professional sport in 1892. The first

15
00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:46.360
football league was established in 1920. Two years later, it changed its name to the NFL

16
00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:53.800
National Football League, which still exists today. After 1958, when a great championship

17
00:01:53.800 --> 00:02:01.080
game was played, football's popularity grew. Now it is the most popular sport in the United States.

18
00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:07.480
The championship, now called the Super Bowl, is watched by more Americans than any other

19
00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:14.760
television event. The game, with its violence, strategy, and passion, is deeply rooted in

20
00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:21.000
American culture.
